Musk does not necessarily need Grok to defeat every rival.

He needs the race to continue building roads.

If Grok wins, he owns the model.

If another model wins, the AI economy still expands.

If AI moves into vehicles, Tesla supplies an endpoint.

If agents spread into remote infrastructure, ships, farms, aircraft, robots and military systems, Starlink’s access layer becomes more valuable.

If orbital compute develops, SpaceX owns the launch vehicle and much of the relevant satellite-operating experience.

If the industry quarrels, the quarrel happens on X.

Musk owns a horse, the starting pistol, the grandstand, the betting shop, the broadcast platform and increasingly the road to the stadium.

Then he stands beside the track warning that horse racing may destroy civilisation.

