4. X Is the Agitation Engine

SpaceX’s prospectus does not describe X as an incidental social network attached to the AI company.

It defines X as a foundational distribution and data engine for the entire AI ecosystem. The combined Grok-and-X platforms reported approximately 550 million monthly active users in March 2026, of whom roughly 117 million had used Grok’s AI features. 

X performs several functions simultaneously:

Public stage
Where the AI race is discussed
Distribution channel
Where Grok is placed in front of users
Data source
Where real-time human reactions are collected
Feedback mechanism
Where outputs are praised, mocked and corrected
Subscription product
Where AI features encourage paid conversion
Advertising surface
Where attention becomes revenue

The prospectus says advertising remains a core monetisation channel and describes a strategy of making ads resemble contextually relevant content integrated into live conversations. It says Grok can support campaign creation, creative optimisation and alignment with trending topics and user intent. 

That creates a beautifully circular system.

Musk posts about AI.

People argue about the post.

The argument increases activity on X.

The activity becomes live context for Grok.

Grok becomes a reason to subscribe to X.

Grok helps advertisers align campaigns with the argument.

Advertising monetises the attention generated by the argument.

The resulting commercial loop is:

\text{Provocation}
\rightarrow
\text{engagement}
\rightarrow
\text{data}
\rightarrow
\text{AI product value}
\rightarrow
\text{subscriptions and advertising}

This does not prove that every Musk post is deliberately calibrated for revenue.

It shows that the platform’s economics reward him whether the provocation was strategic, impulsive, sincere or typed while waiting for a rocket test.

His feed does not need to be a coherent manifesto.

It functions perfectly well as a spark plug.

Watching it is often like watching a man walk through a fireworks warehouse with a cigar, then advertise the live satellite footage of the explosion.

