10. The House Wins Even When Another Horse Wins

Let the useful capability or deployment of AI provider i be C_i.

A conventional AI company’s revenue is dominated by its own model:

R_i \approx f(C_i)

A competitor’s advance usually threatens that company:

\frac{\partial R_i}{\partial C_j}<0
\qquad
j\neq i

Musk’s integrated position is different.

A simplified Musk portfolio is:

R_M =
R_{\text{Grok}}
+
R_X
+
R_{\text{connectivity}}
+
R_{\text{Tesla}}
+
R_{\text{launch}}

A rival model improving may reduce Grok’s relative share:

\frac{\partial R_{\text{Grok}}}{\partial C_j}<0

But the same improvement may:

* increase public attention to AI;
* increase AI usage on X;
* normalise subscriptions and agents;
* produce more connected endpoints;
* increase infrastructure construction;
* increase satellite deployment;
* and enlarge demand for remote communications.

Therefore:

\frac{\partial R_M}{\partial C_j}
=
\frac{\partial R_{\text{Grok}}}{\partial C_j}
+
\frac{\partial R_X}{\partial C_j}
+
\frac{\partial R_{\text{connectivity}}}{\partial C_j}
+
\frac{\partial R_{\text{launch}}}{\partial C_j}
+\cdots

The total may remain positive even when Grok loses model share.

That is the strategic elegance of the arrangement.

If Grok wins

Musk receives subscriptions, enterprise licences, API revenue and data-centre demand.

If OpenAI wins

AI adoption still grows, businesses deploy more agents, consumers discuss the result on X and the connected-machine economy expands.

If open models win

More developers can place AI into local and edge devices, increasing the number of intelligent endpoints that may require communications.

If closed cloud models win

More devices require persistent access to centralised inference.

If governments regulate heavily

Large incumbents with capital, government contracts and existing compliance infrastructure are better positioned than small entrants.

If governments adopt AI militarily

xAI sells models and SpaceX already supplies relevant communications infrastructure.

If orbital AI compute becomes practical

SpaceX plans to launch and operate it.

If orbital AI compute is nonsense

SpaceX still sells terrestrial launch and Starlink connectivity.

Every outcome is not equally valuable.

But Musk has built more ways to collect a toll than the ordinary entrant.

He does not need to correctly predict the winner.

He needs the starting pistol to keep firing.

